WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:02.600
What fresh hell is this?

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:07.120
After a ten-year absence from the silver screen,
Hellboy made his return in a gory two-hour

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.700
reboot of the franchise.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:13.160
Amid all the crushed skulls,the film leaves
several loose ends in its wake, so let's try

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.360
making some sense of that unruly ending.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.540
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.460
Hellboy's titular half-man, half-hellbeast

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:24.410
is portrayed by Stranger Things' David Harbour,
who fills the formidable shoes of Ron Perlman,

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:27.800
the actor who starred in Guillermo del Toro's
Hellboy films.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:32.259
The film grabs imagery from the original comic
book series by Mike Mignola, cribbing plot

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:35.640
points and characters from The Wild Hunt,
among several others.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.140
Hellboy works for the Bureau for Paranormal
Research and Defense, battling supernatural

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:45.280
creepos alongside his adoptive father, Professor
Trevor Bruttenholm, played by Deadwood's Ian

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:45.920
McShane.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:50.140
Throughout the film, Hellboy is hot on the
trail of a spiteful witch named Nimue the

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:53.070
Blood Queen, portrayed by Milla Jovovich.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:57.420
In the flashback sequence that opens the film,
Nimue is chopped to bits by none other than

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:01.070
King Arthur, who rips her apart with his mighty
sword Excalibur.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:06.110
Nimue's body parts are scattered throughout
the land and remain buried for 1,500 years.

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:11.140
Alas, she's eventually pieced back together
by her willing supplicant, the humanoid warthog

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:11.940
Gruagach.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.420
Now, Hellboy must stop Nimue before she destroys
humanity.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.140
Beneath all the rotting flesh and gouged eyeballs,

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.160
this is the story of a creature searching
for his place in the world.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:27.330
If we were to boil down the character's central
dilemma, we'd say he vacillates between sympathizing

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:30.369
with the supernatural world and siding with
humans.

00:01:30.369 --> 00:01:34.700
As the film lunges toward its conclusion,
we learn that Hellboy is the spawn of a demon

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.760
and a witch of Arthurian descent.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:41.560
In the final confrontation, Nimue the Blood
Queen temporarily seduces Hellboy to the dark

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.820
side after killing Professor Bruttenholm before
his eyes.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:49.920
Hellboy is garlanded in a kicky crown of hell-flame
and immediately grows his horns out, because

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:50.740
he's evil now.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.660
As Nimue's squadron of unearthly creatures
rip through the terrified London streets,

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:59.080
Hellboy ultimately comes to his senses and
overpowers Nimue.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:03.880
He decapitates her with Excalibur, sending
her still-screaming head back into the fiery

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:04.880
fathoms of hell.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.700
In the film's final set piece, Hellboy finds
himself on a dangerous mission in Siberia

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:15.670
with two trusty cohorts from the BPRD: scrappy
spirit medium Alice Monaghan, played by Sasha

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:19.160
Lane, and moody Ben Daimio, played by Daniel
Dae Kim.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:25.460
Ben is a downlow were-jaguar whose theoretically
British accent also has a penchant for shapeshifting.

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:29.959
After dispatching the members of a secret
cabal called the Atlantis Society, the trio

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.440
notice a large fish tank.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:35.969
Suddenly, webbed fingers poke out from the
murky water and touch the glass surface.

00:02:35.969 --> 00:02:40.719
If you've ever read the comics or seen the
Guillermo del Toro films, the name Abe Sapien

00:02:40.719 --> 00:02:45.599
will surely mean something to you: Although
he may be half-man and half-amphibian, the

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.340
character is entirely badass.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:52.620
Portrayed by Doug Jones in del Toro's films,
Abe Sapien was once a man named Langdon Everett

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:58.029
who dabbled in the occult and paid the ultimate
price: He became a half-man and half-amphibian

00:02:58.029 --> 00:02:58.740
monstrosity.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:02.699
Those are Abe's webbed fingers, clearly clamouring
for a sequel.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:05.139
"Remind me of why I keep doing this."

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:08.600
Hellboy's ghostly rendezvous
Hellboy throws not one but two scenes into

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:09.700
the end credits.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:13.840
In the mid-credits scene, we find Hellboy
mourning the recent death of Professor Trevor

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:14.340
Bruttenholm.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:18.940
Suddenly the specter of a certain Lobster
Johnson appears, portrayed by actor Thomas

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:19.640
Haden Church.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:23.620
The ghostly figure wastes no time telling
Hellboy: "Evil... it is coming."

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:29.419
Johnson also appears in an earlier flashback,
making mincemeat out of a slew of Nazi occultists.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:30.920
So who is this guy?

00:03:31.109 --> 00:03:35.920
Long story short, he's a beloved character
in the Hellboy universe; a vigilante who plays

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:37.200
by his own rules.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:37.920
"Aah!"

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:39.279
"Guten tag!"

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:42.730
"I love you, Lobster Johnson!"

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:47.939
As you just saw, Johnson is fond of searing
his signature "lobster claw" symbol into the

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:49.280
foreheads of his enemies.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.800
What's not to like about that?

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.000
During his quest to find Nimue the Blood Queen,

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.480
Hellboy pays a visit to Baba Yaga, a haggard
witch who exists in some far-off dimension.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:07.260
Baba Yaga offers Hellboy some clues regarding
Nimue's whereabouts, but this intel comes

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:09.939
at a price: He must give her one of his eyeballs.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:14.400
He agrees, but manages to escape Baba Yaga
with both eyeballs intact.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:19.820
But in a post-credits scene, Baba Yaga convinces
an unseen accomplice to murder Hellboy at

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:24.560
his earliest convenience and hand over the
hellish eye she was promised.The Los Angeles

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:29.900
Times seems to think she's talking to Koschei
the Deathless, a seemingly "immortal" assassin

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:32.280
who appears in the Darkness Falls graphic
novel.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:36.880
This theory gels with the fact that Baba Yaga
assures her henchman she'll mercifully end

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:38.900
his life if he brings her Hellboy's eye.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:43.600
After surviving a movie full of so much sensory
overload, you may be willing to volunteer

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:44.560
both of your own.

